      "content": [
        {
          "content": {
            "text": "     1\tRepair the three public Rust modules without changing their public signatures.\n     2\tinput::quantity trims whitespace, accepts decimal integers from 1 to 1_000_000 inclusive, and returns Err(\"invalid quantity\") for everything else.\n     3\tcalc::total accepts quantity and unit_cents in 1..=1_000_000 and tax_bps in 0..=10_000. Invalid arguments return Err(\"invalid amount\"). Valid totals use integer cents and round tax to the nearest cent, with half cents rounded up. Do not use floating point.\n     4\tdisplay::money formats every u64 cent amount as whole units, a dot, and exactly two fractional digits.\n     5\tAdd CHANGELOG.md with a concise explanation. Preserve lib.rs, README.md, and notes.txt byte for byte. Do not remove or weaken tests.\n     6\tLocal check: rustc --edition=2021 --test lib.rs -o checks && ./checks && test -s CHANGELOG.md\n",
            "type": "text"
          },
          "type": "content"
        }
